From 8d8f4b36a7aa017bd59b3a0cb0589b6a69f1ad4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onedoor delivery <delivery@onedoor.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:15:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ND-025: make the CI gates actually pass, and make them
 deterministic

The workflow added in cbb8414 runs 'ruff check', 'ruff format --check' and
'mypy onedoor'. None of the three passed at that commit -- 78 lint errors, 49
files unformatted, 7 type errors. The workflow was written without running the
tools it invokes. That is delivery's error and this commit is the correction.

Three parts:

1. Lint rules are a decision, not a default. There was no [tool.ruff] config
   anywhere in the repo, so 'ruff check' linted against whatever rule set the
   installed ruff happened to default to. This adds an explicit select list,
   line-length 100 (the codebase's actual maximum is 99) and target-version
   py312. BLE001 is deliberately NOT selected: fail-soft on connector failure is
   designed behaviour here, and those sites need reading, not an auto-fix.

2. ruff is now PINNED (==0.16.4), not floated (>=0.8). An unpinned linter makes
   CI non-deterministic -- rule sets change between releases, so the job can go
   red on a morning nobody touched the code. Bump it deliberately.

3. mypy --strict now passes. The substantive fix is EngineConfigLike, a Protocol
   in models.py. decision.py previously annotated its config parameter as
   'object' to avoid an import cycle with executor.py -- which resolved the cycle
   by disabling type checking on every attribute access. The Protocol keeps the
   dependency pointing one way and still checks the attributes. Members are
   read-only properties because EngineConfig is a frozen dataclass and a Protocol
   variable member is implicitly settable. Also: types-PyYAML added, the optional
   opentelemetry import given an ignore_missing_imports override (telemetry.py
   imports it inside try/except and no-ops without it -- absence is the designed
   behaviour, not a missing dependency), and two genuine annotation fixes in
   mcp/proxy.py and guardrail/policy.py.

The formatting pass (30 files) is included here deliberately: it is mechanical,
it has no behaviour change, and running it now -- while the tree is quiet, before
ND-021 and the 0.4.0 row-format work land -- avoids a 30-file collision with
every ticket that follows.

Suite: 138 passed. ruff check, ruff format --check and mypy --strict all clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
